  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.4.1 - Added the net11.0 target. No API or wire format changes.\n\nv0.4.0 - Protocol design review: hard limits, timeouts, integrity, error codes, telemetry, streaming send, Stream/TLS support.\n\nAdded:\n  * HyperionProtocolOptions.MaxMessageSize (default 1 GiB), ReceiveTimeout / SendTimeout (idle timeouts, default off) and ChunkChecksum (per-chunk CRC-32C: Off / Emit / Required).\n  * HyperionErrorCode on every HyperionProtocolException (InvalidMagic, MessageTooLarge, ChecksumMismatch, Timeout, PeerClosed, ...).\n  * SendStreamingAsync(Stream source, long length, Stream destination): send files of any size without buffering; pairs with ReceiveStreamingAsync.\n  * ReceiveStreamingAsync(PipeReader) and a SmartHyperionProtocol override of ReceiveStreamingAsync that understands all three framings.\n  * HyperionDiagnostics: System.Diagnostics.Metrics counters and ActivitySource spans (OpenTelemetry-ready).\n  * Crc32C helper (SSE4.2 / ARM intrinsics with table fallback).\n  * docs/DESIGN.md, docs/SPECIFICATION.md and docs/DESIGN_CHECKLIST.md.\n\nChanged:\n  * All NetworkStream parameters are now Stream, so SslStream (TLS), named pipes and in-memory streams work directly. Source-compatible for callers; subclasses overriding the old signatures must update them.\n  * Receivers enforce the uniform-chunk rule (all non-final chunks carry the size of chunk 0) and MaxMessageSize, both before reading payload bytes.\n  * A clean disconnect at a message boundary is reported as HyperionErrorCode.PeerClosed; a disconnect mid-frame as UnexpectedEndOfStream; ReceiveStreamingAsync now wraps EOF the same way as the buffered paths.\n  * Header JSON is produced by a System.Text.Json source generator (no reflection on the hot path).\n\nWire format: unchanged and backward compatible with 0.1.x-0.3.x. The optional \"Crc32C\" header member is ignored by older receivers.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/TechTeaStudio/HyperionProtocol/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
